    "body": "I was able to successfully run the `UseCase1_BasicSelection` example on Windows and debug it step-by-step. I've noted a few points regarding exception handling and behavior on Windows.\n\n---\n\n### Issues & Observations\n\n* **Unhandled Exceptions:** Unlike Java, when exceptions occur in C++, the program hangs without any output. I added a global `try/catch` block in the `main` function to capture all exceptions and display the error, which works but might not be the most elegant solution. It would be helpful to have a more robust way to handle these exceptions and provide a stack trace.\n\n* **PCSC on Windows:** When no card readers are connected, the PC/SC implementation on Windows throws a `\"Could not access terminals list\"` exception instead of returning an empty list. This is likely because the Windows service is only active when a reader is present. This behavior seems to be different from Linux. We should consider handling this exception to provide a better user experience.\n\n---\n\n### Positive Feedback\n\n* **APDU Exchanges:** When a reader and an EMV card are connected, the APDU exchanges work perfectly.",
